title: Song Bie (Farewell)
artist: John P. Ordway / Li Shutong
origin: China
culture: Chinese
genre: Folk
language: zh
key: C major
tempo: 92
meter: 4/4
pickup: 0
intro: 2
outro: 1
style: asian
guide: flute
year: 1915
attribution: Chinese farewell song with words written about 1915 by Li Shutong (Master Hongyi, died 1942) to the melody of John P. Ordway's "Dreaming of Home and Mother" (published 1868; Ordway died in 1880), in the simplified form of the 1907 Japanese school song "Ryoshū" by Kyūkei Indō (died 1943). The words were printed in 1927. Melody and words are public domain.
source_url: https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/送别_(歌曲)
tags: china, farewell, friendship, school song

chords:
| C | F C | C | G7 | C | F C | G7 | C |
| F | G7 C | F C | G7 | C | F C | G7 | C |

melody:
cháng tíng wài, gǔ dào biān,
= 长 亭 外， 古 道 边，
G4 E4/ ~G4/ C5(2) A4 C5 G4(2)
fāng cǎo bì lián tiān.
= 芳 草 碧 连 天。
G4 C4/ ~D4/ E4 D4/ ~C4/ D4(3) r
wǎn fēng fú liǔ dí shēng cán,
= 晚 风 拂 柳 笛 声 残，
G4 E4/ ~G4/ C5. B4/ A4 C5 G4(2)
xī yáng shān wài shān.
= 夕 阳 山 外 山。
G4 D4/ ~E4/ F4. B3/ C4(3) r
tiān zhī yá, dì zhī jiǎo,
= 天 之 涯， 地 之 角，
A4 C5 C5(2) B4 A4/ ~B4/ C5(2)
zhī jiāo bàn líng luò.
= 知 交 半 零 落。
A4/ ~B4/ C5/ ~A4/ A4/ ~G4/ E4/ ~C4/ D4(3) r
yī piáo zhuó jiǔ jìn yú huān,
= 一 瓢 浊 酒 尽 余 欢，
G4 E4/ ~G4/ C5. B4/ A4 C5 G4(2)
jīn xiāo bié mèng hán.
= 今 宵 别 梦 寒。
G4 D4/ ~E4/ F4. B3/ C4(3) r
